{%- comment -%}
  The runtime shipping-copy patch (snippets/lbass-copy-fix.liquid) was rendered
  here and is now DELETED — 2026-08-05. Every figure it corrected at runtime is
  fixed at source, so nothing needs patching after paint:

    templates/index.liquid       announcement strip 299 → 500  (line ~883)
                                 delivery accordion  40 → 30   (line ~1782)
                                 FAQPage JSON-LD     40 → 30   (line ~1899)
    templates/product.liquid     .pdpx-note          40 → 30   (line ~356)
                                 .acc-body           40 → 30   (line ~574)
    snippets/lbass-cart-drawer   .lbdr-ship          40 → 30   (line ~150)

  The JSON-LD instance is why deleting the patch mattered rather than being
  cosmetic. A DOM patch can only rewrite text nodes; it could never reach an
  answer string inside <script type="application/ld+json">. So while the
  visible page was being corrected to 30, the homepage's structured data still
  told Google 40 — schema disagreeing with the page it describes.

  These were only editable because the theme was pulled with the Shopify CLI
  and edited on disk. The Admin API has no partial write, so changing one line
  in a 226KB template means round-tripping all of it. If a rate changes again,
  use `shopify theme pull` — do not reintroduce a runtime patch.
{%- endcomment -%}

